WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.250
If you’re in a Final Destination movie,
your best hope of surviving is to look for

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:04.250
the signs.

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:07.140
Right from the opening credits, there are
signs of impending danger, like the scissors

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.990
pointed at Kimberly’s head in this photo,
or the blade directed at her face right next

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:11.990
to that.

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:15.050
Kimberly has an eye on her keychain, a clue
that she will be the clairvoyant whose vision

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:18.850
saves the lives of several people, and when
she first wakes up that afternoon, the time

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:23.300
is 1:08, an anagram of 180, referencing the
flight number of the big accident from the

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.300
first movie.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:28.160
There would be many other appearances of the
ominous number 180, as well as many other

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:29.619
signs that often go unnoticed.

00:00:29.619 --> 00:00:33.470
To hear about every last secret, stick around
to the end of this video.

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:37.730
This video is sponsored by Hunt a Killer.

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:40.130
[INTRO]

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:44.000
Welcome to Things You Missed and if you’re
watching on upload day, Happy Halloween.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.870
This year’s Halloween may not be what we’re
used to, but hopefully you found a way to

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:47.870
enjoy it.

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:49.590
Final Destination 2 brought in a new director.

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:53.810
James Wong handed it over to David R. Ellis,
who was mostly known for work in the stunt

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:58.060
department -- so the result was… one really
cool spectacle at the beginning of the movie,

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:01.030
but a lot of… weird stuff for the rest of
the film.

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:02.980
“A man with hooks…

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:05.409
I think I see a man with hooks.”

00:01:05.409 --> 00:01:08.059
We’ll get into that, but first, let’s
get into the Things You Missed.

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:10.374
"You missed that? Aw!"

00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:19.179
Kimberly first wakes up at the beginning of
the movie when she hears a strange voice utter

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:20.179
her name.

00:01:20.179 --> 00:01:21.179
“Kimberly.”

00:01:21.179 --> 00:01:25.490
I believe this is the voice the coroner, William
Bludworth, who later somehow know her name

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:29.210
when Clear brings her to the morgue to ask
questions about death, suggesting that William

00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:32.110
could be much more than a creepy dude who
knows a lot about death.

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:35.569
This is effectively the first sign that she
actually notices about the tragedy that would

00:01:35.569 --> 00:01:37.780
become known as the Route 23 pile-up.

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:40.720
The next is when her door suddenly closes.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:43.459
In the past we’ve seen that Death is often
associated with the wind.

00:01:43.459 --> 00:01:47.060
Her an her friends are headed off on a road
trip to Daytona Beach, a parallel to the first

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:50.060
movie, where Flight 180 is also a travel related
accident.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:53.740
When she drives away, her car is leaking transmission
fluid that almost looks like blood.

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:57.340
In our Flight 180 analogy, the equivalent
of the airport terminal would be the highway

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:01.420
on-ramp, and just as Alex is disturbed by
a creepy missionary, Kimberly is startled

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:05.689
by a creepy old woman collecting trash, which
her friend Dano finds way funnier than it

00:02:05.689 --> 00:02:06.816
actually is.

00:02:06.816 --> 00:02:09.467
*laughter*

00:02:09.539 --> 00:02:10.539
Ok.

00:02:10.539 --> 00:02:13.121
They get on the highway and see a school bus
transporting a sports team.

00:02:13.121 --> 00:02:17.040
There’s a banner that says Demolish the
Mustangs… smoke their butts -- and later

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:21.180
down the road they would encounter a Ford
Mustang with smoke coming out of the butt,

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:22.810
and it gets demolished in the accident.

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:26.599
We see the bus for realsies after the premonition,
and learn that it’s a bus from Mt. Abraham

00:02:26.599 --> 00:02:30.629
High School, which is the school from whose
French class fatally boarded Flight 180.

00:02:30.629 --> 00:02:34.819
Alex Browning encountered a couple of references
to hell and demons before boarding that plane,

00:02:34.819 --> 00:02:38.590
and when Kimberly changes the radio station,
AC/DC’s “Highway to Hell” starts playing,

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:42.760
which coincidentally I used to sing every
day in 6th grade on my way to English class.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:46.700
Dano tosses his ILLEGAL SUBSTANCE joint out
the window and it lands on the windshield

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:49.689
of a woman named Kat, where it burns some
leaves that are stuck there.

00:02:49.689 --> 00:02:54.299
This could either be a sign of the fiery explosions
caused by the pile-up, or any of the other four

00:02:54.299 --> 00:02:56.120
other fiery explosions in the film.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:59.690
The real scariest part of this movie is just
the fact that like 50% of the people on this

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:01.790
road are driving under the influence.

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:05.360
Between Kat, Rory, and this truck driver,
it’s a wonder that it took five whole minutes

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:07.079
for a major accident to occur.

00:03:07.079 --> 00:03:10.910
By the way, the drinking driver represents
a company called Hice Pale Ale, a reference

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:12.769
to stunt co-ordinator Freddie Hice.

00:03:12.769 --> 00:03:15.909
You probably didn’t miss the weird kid smashing
together the toy cars.

00:03:15.909 --> 00:03:17.480
I mean who does that?

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:21.140
But what you may not have noticed is that
it’s a red truck crashing into a big blue

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:24.520
commercial vehicle, which is not only what
happens at the end of Kimberly’s vision,

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:28.519
but also what happens for real, when Kimberly
loses her friends after stepping out of the

00:03:28.519 --> 00:03:29.519
vehicle.

00:03:29.519 --> 00:03:32.879
The truck that starts the big pile up in Kimberly’s
vision has a loose wire hanging off of it,

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:36.659
which brings back memories of the end of the
first movie, where a similar wire almost caused

00:03:36.659 --> 00:03:38.860
the death of the main characters Clear and
Alex.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:42.180
This truck also has a familiar license plate
VKY 722.

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:46.170
We last saw this plate in my Things You Missed
episode on Stephen King’s Misery, where

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:49.709
it was the license plate of Paul Sheldon’s
car, and I mentioned it has appeared in many

00:03:49.709 --> 00:03:52.549
movies, like The Freshman, Shaft and The Wolf
of Wall Street.

00:03:52.549 --> 00:03:56.180
Finally, after the premonition, when the real
accident occurs, Kimberly looks up and sees

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:59.930
a sign that says, “Warning Work Ahead: Next 180 Feet.”

00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:05.670
This is the number 180 resurfacing as it has
so many times since Flight 180, as I discussed

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:06.170
when I covered the first movie.

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:08.290
The new number added to the mix this time
is number 23.

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:10.420
In addition to the accident taking place on
Route 23, Kimberly notices that the next service

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:15.050
station is 23 miles away after her Dad calls
to warn about her car’s leak.

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:19.380
Final Destination 2 is pretty much the same
exact movie as the first, with one key difference.

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:23.630
This time William Bludworth tells them that
the only way to defeat death is with new life,

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:27.080
so the majority of the film is spent trying
to make sure nothing bad happens to this woman,

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:30.960
Isabella, so she can safely deliver her baby,
and theoretically force Death to completely

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:32.060
reset its list.

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:35.470
There’s a scene later on where we learn
that each character is connected by the fact

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:38.530
that they should have died at some point over
the last year, but each of them missed their

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:41.690
appointment with death because of one of the
Flight 180 survivors.

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:45.470
At the end, Isabella is revealed not to have
been on Death’s list yet, but that doesn’t

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:47.200
mean she isn’t connected to the others.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:51.080
We first see her in the premonition driving
her white van, which has a logo for Fresh

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:52.139
and Fast Florist.

00:04:52.139 --> 00:04:55.970
In other words, she’s delivering flowers,
and I think the reason she’s there, is because

00:04:55.970 --> 00:04:59.650
she’s delivering to the 1 year anniversary
memorial at Mt. Abraham High School that we

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:01.040
hear about on the radio.

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:07.190
“...candlelight vigil to mark the 1 year
anniversary of the crash of Flight 180, will

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:10.660
be held at 8PM tonight at the Mt. Abraham
High School auditorium.”

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:13.240
After the premonition, there’s even a part
where she asks to get through because she

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:14.240
has to make a delivery.

00:05:15.783 --> 00:05:19.367
“Excuse me, is there any way that we could
drive around?

00:05:19.367 --> 00:05:22.080
I have a delivery--”
“You need to get back into your vehicles.”

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:25.840
I think that fate had her making this delivery
because Death wanted Clear to be lured out

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:29.759
of hiding, and needed her to end up at the
Lakeview Hospital when Eugene’s room exploded.

00:05:29.759 --> 00:05:31.749
It’s all part of Death’s design.

00:05:31.749 --> 00:05:36.960
But there would be many more accidents before
then, each with clues of their own to uncover.

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:44.920
The holiday we've been waiting for all year
has finally arrived and if you’re like me,

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:48.020
you’ve found something scary to enjoy at
home this year because of COVID-19.

00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:52.490
And if you’re like me, you’re looking
to keep things scary all year round.

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:55.759
Something that I’ve been enjoying to fill
that Halloween void is Hunt a Killer’s Blair

00:05:55.759 --> 00:05:56.759
Witch game.

