00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:48.160
There’s a running theme of luck and chance
in Final Destination 2.

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:50.629
The dice hanging from Rory’s mirror, represent
chance.

00:06:50.629 --> 00:06:54.980
The police chief considers each of the survivors
to very lucky, especially Evan Lewis, who

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:56.690
won the lottery the previous day.

00:06:56.690 --> 00:06:59.960
Ironically his last words are, “**** I’m
lucky,” before getting crushed by a falling

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:00.960
ladder.

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:03.789
Walking under a ladder is considered back
luck, and so are black cats.

00:07:03.789 --> 00:07:07.592
During Evan’s incident he tries cooking
lunch for himself using Black Cat Cooking Oil.

00:07:07.685 --> 00:07:09.864
And Evan's new ring is a horseshoe ring, 

00:07:09.864 --> 00:07:11.864
which is considered to be a lucky charm.

00:07:11.864 --> 00:07:15.116
Also, that's the only reason the Colts won the Super Bowl in 2007.

00:07:15.116 --> 00:07:19.560
The number 13 is considered to be the unlucky
number and it can be seen on Eugene’s billiard

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:20.560
ball keychain.

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:23.410
This ball starts a chain reaction that nearly
gets someone killed.

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:28.243
When we first see this ball on his keychain,
Eugene is also 13th accident survivor on Death's list.

00:07:28.243 --> 00:07:32.250
Officer Burke is a policeman who is part of
unit 13.

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:37.563
“This is Unit 13 requesting medical assistance
…”

00:07:37.563 --> 00:07:40.310
"Let's go practice medicine."

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:44.550
The first individual accident scene in the
movie is Mr. Lucky himself, Evan Lewis.

00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:47.610
We see him after he’s just used some of
his lotto money to buy expensive stuff.

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:51.669
In the hallway outside of his apartment, there
are a number of signs: a pile-up of toy cars

00:07:51.669 --> 00:07:55.229
and vehicles was probably his first sign about
the incident on Route 23.

00:07:55.229 --> 00:07:59.479
He nearly steps on a toy ambulance that says
Mt. Pleasant on the side, which is identical

00:07:59.479 --> 00:08:02.139
to the ambulance that picks him up after his
accident.

00:08:02.139 --> 00:08:05.970
He nearly falls after stepping on this one
eyed baby doll, which isn’t a Toy Story

00:08:05.970 --> 00:08:09.229
reference, it’s an omen about Evan’s eventual
fate, where the fire escape ladder punctures

00:08:09.229 --> 00:08:10.229
his right eye.

00:08:10.229 --> 00:08:13.389
There’s another clue about that in his kitchen,
where the refrigerator magnets seem to spell

00:08:13.389 --> 00:08:17.310
out “HEYE”, but the H falls away, (think
of a ladder as a bunch of H’s stacked on

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:20.889
top of one another) and the result is the
word EYE, which is what get poked out when

00:08:20.889 --> 00:08:22.069
that ladder falls.

00:08:22.069 --> 00:08:23.660
And the new computer he buys is an iMac.

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:24.660
Not a nose-Mac.

00:08:24.660 --> 00:08:25.660
Not a chin-Mac.

00:08:25.660 --> 00:08:26.810
An iMac.

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:31.000
The song he puts on is called Vitamin by the
band Incubus who are named after the Latin-derived

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:34.870
word Incubus, which refers to a male-demon,
another one of the demonic references I mentioned

00:08:34.870 --> 00:08:35.870
earlier.

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:37.169
It goes along well with his demon-tail necklace.

00:08:37.169 --> 00:08:40.909
He also has this monkey-demon statue sitting
by his window, which is next to a miniature

00:08:40.909 --> 00:08:46.620
version of his 1979 Pontiac Trans Am, which you may remember
had a Phoenix decal on its hood.

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:49.130
He also has the firebird image on his front
door.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:52.500
These are all signs that he’s going to start
a fire in the apartment, which ultimately

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:53.930
leads him to his death.

00:08:53.930 --> 00:08:57.131
The mozzarella sticks he cooks are from a
company called “Surefire Snacks,” which

00:08:57.131 --> 00:08:59.630
sure-enough is the catalyst of that apartment
fire.

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:03.570
I would also say that this Incubus song is
fire, but they wouldn’t have called it that

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:05.880
back then, so I won’t count that one.

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:08.450
I’m just surprised they didn’t use “Pardon
Me.”

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:12.584
“A decade ago. I never thought I would be
At twenty-three, on the verge of

00:09:12.584 --> 00:09:14.364
Spontaneous combustion, woe is me.”

00:09:14.364 --> 00:09:18.360
After Evan’s over-the-top ending to depth
perception, Officer Burke looks up more info

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:22.920
on Flight 180 and comes across a website about
plane crash survivors, which has photos of

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:26.540
each of the survivors, and for some reason
the photo of Tod is captioned as “A nice

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:28.589
shot before the coroner arrived.”

00:09:28.589 --> 00:09:29.589
What is nice about that?

00:09:29.589 --> 00:09:31.230
It’s a dead 17 year old.

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:34.570
Also, I noticed that their supposed “high
school photos” are almost definitely taken

00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:38.790
from the photoshoot for Final Destination
1’s poster and just given a different background.

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:43.600
Various characters learn the news of Evan’s
death, including Kat, who is smoking on the

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:44.600
treadmill?

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:45.600
What is the point of that?

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:47.339
That would be like if I made a video but didn’t
upload it.

00:09:47.339 --> 00:09:51.330
But there is an interesting painting near
Eugene’s TV of what seems to be a person

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:55.210
with their legs severed from the rest of their
body, a hint about Rory, who later gets his

00:09:55.210 --> 00:09:57.279
legs cut off by the wire fence.

00:09:57.279 --> 00:10:01.700
The child, Tim, is reading Stephen King’s
Bag of Bones before bed -- which is novel about

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:05.610
a writer who has disturbing dreams and visions,
much like Kimberly does in this movie.

00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:09.260
Speaking of Kimberly, she has a few interesting
items of her own that I haven’t mentioned

00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:12.010
yet, because they’re connections to things
outside of this movie.

00:10:12.010 --> 00:10:15.269
For example, one of the first things we see
in her room is a puppet, which I think was

00:10:15.269 --> 00:10:19.120
a reference a cut line from Mr.
Bludworth that can only be seen in the deleted

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:20.120
scenes.

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:30.170
“But be warned, to disrupt the grand design
is to unravel the tapestry of the universe.

00:10:30.170 --> 00:10:39.250
And when you pull those threads apart, you
might find yourself hanging from them.”

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:43.290
I also noticed a picture of a bridge in her
room, which of course makes me think about

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:47.421
the opening disaster in Final Destination
5, even if it wasn’t an intentional reference

00:10:47.421 --> 00:10:48.421
at the time.

00:10:48.421 --> 00:10:50.200
There’s also a clown on a trapeze in her
room.

00:10:50.200 --> 00:10:52.050
Makes me think of another scene from the fifth
one.

00:10:52.050 --> 00:10:55.760
There’s another link to a later movie in
the franchise when Nora takes her son to the

00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:58.269
dentist’s office and a fish gets stuck in
the filter.

00:10:58.269 --> 00:11:01.600
We see a very similar accident happen in the
fourth movie.

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:05.139
Before that happens though, Kimberly goes
talk to the only remaining Flight 180 survivor,

00:11:05.139 --> 00:11:06.139
Clear.

00:11:06.139 --> 00:11:09.840
There’s a lot more info here about what
happened to Clear in between Final Destination

00:11:09.840 --> 00:11:13.440
1 and Final Destination 2, so I did a whole
video on it, which you can check out right

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:14.850
here if you’re interested.

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:17.040
There are also some names written on the side
here.

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:21.130
The first three are Flight 180 victims, who
if you’ve seen my episode on the first movie,

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:22.130
you know are named after crew members.

00:11:22.130 --> 00:11:26.360
The other two names aren’t credits, but
they appear to be other Hollywood connections,

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:29.649
for example, this guy worked on The Butterfly
Effect which is written by the same guy who

00:11:29.649 --> 00:11:33.720
did Final Destination 2 so I think these could
have been other Flight 180 victims whose names

00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:35.250
were just off-screen here.

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:39.399
One headline that caught my attention was
this one: Hollywood Jumps on Flight 180 Bandwagon.

00:11:39.399 --> 00:11:44.639
So does that mean the movie Final Destination
also exists within the universe of Final Destination?

00:11:44.639 --> 00:11:46.019
Is that what they’re saying here?

00:11:46.019 --> 00:11:49.600
After talking to Clear and seeing some birds
in a window reflection, Kimberly makes this

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:50.600
conclusion:

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:56.040
“If Clear’s right about the order then
Nora and Tim are gonna be attacked by pigeons.”

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:58.870
OK, that’s a pretty big jump to make, but
whatever.

00:11:58.870 --> 00:12:02.330
But that leads us to the next disaster scene,
which starts when we see a skull in the fish

00:12:02.330 --> 00:12:04.980
tank -- the first clue that someone is going
to die here.

00:12:04.980 --> 00:12:07.710
The next clue can not be seen, but only heard.

00:12:07.710 --> 00:12:12.090
The music playing in the waiting room is a
MIDI cover of John Denver’s Rocky Mountain,

00:12:12.090 --> 00:12:15.380
the song that showed up over and over before
each disaster in the first movie.

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:19.006
I’m gonna crack up the volume and roll it.

00:12:19.006 --> 00:12:31.677
🎵 Rocky Mountain High (cover) 🎵

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:37.290
In the dentist’s office there are tanks
of nitrous oxide and oxygen used for laughing

00:12:37.290 --> 00:12:38.290
gas.

00:12:38.290 --> 00:12:41.740
This could be seen as a foreshadowing of the
explosive oxygen tanks that kill Clear and

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:43.180
Eugene at the end of the movie.

00:12:43.180 --> 00:12:46.577
The way Tim dies really doesn’t make any sense
to me, like he sees it but doesn’t try to

00:12:46.577 --> 00:12:47.308
move?

00:12:47.308 --> 00:12:49.608
No one would have that reaction if they see
something falling on them.

00:12:49.608 --> 00:12:54.050
But Tim’s death, as ridiculous as it may
seem, is nowhere near as outlandish as his

00:12:54.050 --> 00:12:55.050
mother’s.

00:12:55.050 --> 00:12:56.450
Death would arrive for her, not long after.

00:13:01.319 --> 00:13:03.070
 
Here are a couple more things I love about

00:13:03.070 --> 00:13:04.750
Hunt a Killer's Blair Witch box.

00:13:04.750 --> 00:13:05.750
The lore.

00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:08.519
This isn't just a generic game of Clue with
a Blair Witch logo slapped on it.

00:13:08.519 --> 00:13:11.990
They actually partnered with the studio Lionsgate
to make something that fits into the Blair

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:13.139
Witch universe.

00:13:13.139 --> 00:13:15.890
Everything they send you feels like it belongs
in a Blair Witch movie.

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:17.770
So everything feels very immersive.

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:21.140
If you love Things You Missed, you'll love
looking out for those little clues, it's a

00:13:21.140 --> 00:13:23.290
great feeling whenever you unlock a new discovery.

00:13:23.290 --> 00:13:24.290
The flexibility.

00:13:24.290 --> 00:13:26.050
There are so many different ways you can play.

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:30.500
I had a fun time with it just playing by myself,
but there are so many clues and materials,

00:13:30.500 --> 00:13:33.980
you could easily team up with a partner or
roommate, or even get a small group together

00:13:33.980 --> 00:13:36.460
for a little teamthink sesh over video chat.

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:39.921
Unlike most ARGs, you're not just staring
at a screen the whole time, so it’s kind

00:13:39.921 --> 00:13:44.120
of perfect for someone like me who has a job
where you’re staring at a screen 16 hours

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:45.120
a day.

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:49.610
You're gonna be getting a 20% discount using
my link, which you can find in the description.

00:13:49.610 --> 00:13:54.240
That's Hunt a Killer dot com slash CZsWorld
and use code: CZsWorld for 20% off.

00:13:58.490 --> 00:14:02.240
In my previous episode, I mentioned how a
lot of Final Destination characters are named

00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:06.760
after great classic horror filmmakers, and
Final Destination 2 is no exception.

00:14:06.760 --> 00:14:11.040
Kimberly Corman and her dad, Mr. Corman, are
named after Roger Corman; Evan Lewis is named

00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:15.339
after Herschel Gordon Lewis and Nora and Tim
Carpenter are named after John Carpenter.

00:14:15.339 --> 00:14:19.820
Tim’s dentist is named Dr. Lees, which could
be in honor of Christopher Lee, one of the

00:14:19.820 --> 00:14:23.529
most iconic actors to play Dracula, and on
Burke’s computer screen, you can spot an

00:14:23.529 --> 00:14:27.339
incident report on Barker Avenue, possibly
a nod to Clive Barker.

00:14:27.339 --> 00:14:31.209
After the construction crew discovers little
Timmy isn’t a load bearing wall, Clear joins

00:14:31.209 --> 00:14:35.060
back up with Kimberly and Burke to take them
to William Bludworth to try and get some answers.

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:37.838
Wait, look at this, is Bludworth an Apostasy
fan?

00:14:37.838 --> 00:14:40.699
*SCREAM*

00:14:40.699 --> 00:14:42.472
Good for him! I always though he was kind of metal.

00:14:42.472 --> 00:14:45.920
Clear’s alertness prevents a possible explosion
at the gas station afterwards, which would

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:50.760
only be a temporary dodge, because as I mentioned,
she does end up dying by explosion.

00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:52.480
Actually, kind of a lot of people do in this movie.

00:14:52.480 --> 00:14:56.030
It is there that they figure out Mr. Bludworth’s
cryptic clue.

00:14:56.030 --> 00:14:59.200
CLEAR: “A brand new soul that was never
part of Death’s design.”

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:02.519
KIMBERLY: “It throws the whole list out
of whack and we start over with a clean slate.”

00:15:02.519 --> 00:15:04.828
BURKE: “Seems like a bit of a reach don’t
you think?”

00:15:04.828 --> 00:15:05.328
Yes!

00:15:05.328 --> 00:15:06.128
Thank you!

00:15:06.128 --> 00:15:10.030
This is where the movie completely turns into
basically a joke.

00:15:10.030 --> 00:15:13.321
They already tried the whole pregnancy thing
where new life that was never meant to be

00:15:13.321 --> 00:15:16.060
can force death to start over in the first
movie.

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:19.680
They were gonna have Clear get pregnant and
have Alex’s baby, but they showed it at

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:22.160
test screenings, it didn’t go over well.

00:15:22.160 --> 00:15:25.779
“The whole baby thing they didn’t like;
it was part of the way Alex and

00:15:25.779 --> 00:15:28.649
Clear didn’t work and they didn’t buy
the baby at the end, they thought it was goofy

00:15:28.649 --> 00:15:30.290
and wasn’t satisfying enough.”

00:15:30.290 --> 00:15:34.730
So why in the **** did they decide to try
it AGAIN in the second movie?

00:15:34.730 --> 00:15:35.779
It makes no sense.

00:15:35.779 --> 00:15:39.780
So they look back at Burke’s cop car cam
to try to find out who Isabella is, and just

00:15:39.780 --> 00:15:43.610
to show you kind of how sloppy this movie
is, according to the camera it’s 9:12 AM

00:15:43.610 --> 00:15:47.610
when they’re on the ramp, but when it happened
the first time it was about 8:16AM, and then

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:50.339
when we see it again after the premonition,
it’s 8:24AM.

00:15:50.339 --> 00:15:54.750
And then it gets much worse at the meeting
that Burke hosts for Route 23 survivors, because

00:15:54.750 --> 00:15:58.691
Rory just completely forgets about personal
boundaries on the elevator.

00:15:59.427 --> 00:16:01.817
“Is that dog **** dude?”

00:16:05.712 --> 00:16:08.586
“You got something right there…

00:16:08.586 --> 00:16:10.520
Here, I can get it for you.”

00:16:10.520 --> 00:16:13.209
“No, it’s OK. It's alright.”

00:16:15.075 --> 00:16:17.700
“Just, let me do it."

00:16:18.054 --> 00:16:22.319
Very weird, but also… did you notice the
elevator music?

00:16:22.319 --> 00:16:26.079
It’s a little hard to tell, but there’s
an elevator music version of Rocky Mountain

00:16:26.079 --> 00:16:27.079
High.

00:16:27.079 --> 00:16:28.232
I’m gonna play back the exact part.

00:16:28.232 --> 00:16:33.745
🎵 Colorado Rocky Mountain high. 🎵

00:16:33.745 --> 00:16:38.819
🎵 Rocky Mountain High (cover) 🎵

00:16:38.819 --> 00:16:42.810
So they have the meeting, and Eugene is just
denying the whole death curse thing, I honestly

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:47.209
don’t even know why he came to the meeting,
cause he just mocks them the entire time, and then he leaves.

00:16:47.209 --> 00:16:50.600
Clear explains that they need to be looking
for signs, and the rest of them try to safe-proof

00:16:50.600 --> 00:16:53.480
the apartment, like Alex did to Clear’s
cabin in the first movie.

00:16:53.480 --> 00:16:58.009
Nora and Eugene get into the elevator with
this weird guy, and to this day I still don’t

00:16:58.009 --> 00:17:00.829
understand why he’s holding this stuff,
or what it even is.

00:17:00.829 --> 00:17:04.220
Are we supposed to understand what’s going
on here even?

00:17:04.220 --> 00:17:05.310
“Whoa…

00:17:12.129 --> 00:17:15.430
A man with hooks.

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:16.947
A man with hooks.

00:17:16.947 --> 00:17:19.425
Hey, I think I see a man with hooks.”

00:17:19.425 --> 00:17:20.730
What does he think they’re gonna say?

00:17:20.730 --> 00:17:22.240
OMG, he’s right!

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:22.922
CLEAR: “Oh my God…

00:17:22.922 --> 00:17:23.814
He’s right!”

00:17:23.814 --> 00:17:24.562
No!!!

00:17:24.562 --> 00:17:25.562
Come on!

00:17:25.562 --> 00:17:26.582
I was kidding!

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:32.835
Oh…

00:17:32.835 --> 00:17:36.750
Oh, I’m sorry, was it not already weird
enough that this guy -- who we’ve never

00:17:36.750 --> 00:17:39.600
seen before -- is holding a bunch of limbs
with hooks on them?

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:41.690
Just pause it right there.

00:17:44.902 --> 00:17:46.188
*sigh*

00:17:48.270 --> 00:17:51.260
So they try calling Nora to warn her about
the man with hooks.

00:17:51.260 --> 00:17:53.160
So let’s break down this phone call.

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:54.630
“Hello?”
“Nora!”

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:55.750
“Who is this?”

00:17:55.750 --> 00:17:58.260
OK, so this establishes that she doesn’t
know who’s calling.

00:17:58.260 --> 00:18:01.370
Rather than saying, “It’s Officer Burke”,
he just starts screaming.

00:18:01.370 --> 00:18:01.870
“NORA!

00:18:01.870 --> 00:18:02.580
CAN YOU HEAR ME?”

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:05.453
Even though she’s given no indication that
she’s having trouble hearing up to this

00:18:05.453 --> 00:18:06.453
point.

00:18:06.920 --> 00:18:10.170
“Officer Burke, I can’t, I can’t hear
you, what?”

00:18:10.170 --> 00:18:13.220
Well if she can’t hear him, how does she
now know who’s calling?

00:18:13.220 --> 00:18:15.300
And also he still hasn’t said who’s calling!

00:18:15.300 --> 00:18:17.360
“A man with hooks is gonna kill you!”

00:18:17.360 --> 00:18:19.220
So she just drops the phone.

00:18:19.220 --> 00:18:20.260
Not asking what that means.

00:18:20.260 --> 00:18:22.810
Not asking for more details, not asking for
elaboration.

00:18:22.810 --> 00:18:24.401
And then she immediately dies.

00:18:24.401 --> 00:18:26.537
*SCREAMS*

00:18:26.537 --> 00:18:30.450
There’s more like Eugene running upstairs
and suddenly having a meltdown where he tries

00:18:30.450 --> 00:18:33.780
to shoot himself, but all of the bullets are
duds, supposedly because it’s not his turn

00:18:33.780 --> 00:18:34.780
to die.

00:18:34.780 --> 00:18:37.310
So are we supposed to believe that he’s
just invincible until the others die?

00:18:37.310 --> 00:18:38.580
I mean, that makes no sense.

00:18:38.580 --> 00:18:42.220
Cause if that’s the case, keep Kat in the
padded room and send Eugene out to do the

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:43.220
rest of the tasks.

00:18:43.220 --> 00:18:44.500
If they do that, they’ve essentially won.

00:18:44.500 --> 00:18:47.770
But yeah, it seems like they do have to die
in order, because later on there’s this

00:18:47.770 --> 00:18:51.340
part where Death knocks down a tree branch
to move Burke out of the way so he doesn't

00:18:51.340 --> 00:18:53.560
get killed by the flying fence that kills
Rory.

00:18:53.560 --> 00:18:57.280
So with that in mind, the plan that makes
the LEAST sense, is sending them all in a

00:18:57.280 --> 00:19:00.140
car together, with Kat, who is next on the
list…

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:01.650
AS THE DRIVER.

00:19:01.650 --> 00:19:03.370
So naturally, that’s exactly what they do.

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:06.920
So at this point, I’m gonna take a break,
I’m gonna calm down, and then we can hopefully

00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:10.000
get through the rest of this movie and the
rest of the Things You Missed.

00:19:19.160 --> 00:19:23.460
In the episode on the first Final Destination,
I pointed out how all of the disasters manufactured

00:19:23.460 --> 00:19:27.420
by death were somehow related to water or
liquid, and that trend continues for most

00:19:27.420 --> 00:19:29.410
of the accidents in Final Destination 2.

00:19:29.410 --> 00:19:33.380
In the opening disaster, the Route 23 pile-up,
we can see that the ground is wet, and water

00:19:33.380 --> 00:19:35.140
is spraying off of everyone’s tires.

00:19:35.140 --> 00:19:38.050
Obviously that prevented the cars from braking
when they should have, which helped make the

00:19:38.050 --> 00:19:42.180
disaster worse, but perhaps even more dangerous
than that is what goes on in Nora and Tim’s

00:19:42.180 --> 00:19:43.180
car.

00:19:43.180 --> 00:19:46.220
When we first see them, Tim is drumming on
the glove compartment with a couple of water

00:19:46.220 --> 00:19:49.530
bottles, and when the pile-up occurs, one
of them falls under Nora’s brake pedal,

00:19:49.530 --> 00:19:52.810
so she’s unable to stop her car from smashing
into what’s ahead of them.

00:19:52.810 --> 00:19:55.930
Evan’s fatal scene doesn’t really have
any water, but I will note that things start

00:19:55.930 --> 00:19:59.199
really going bad for him when he gets his
hand stuck in the garbage disposal in his

00:19:59.199 --> 00:19:59.822
sink.

00:19:59.822 --> 00:20:03.400
Tim’s accident occurs at the dentist, starting
with when the fish tank springs a leak out

00:20:03.400 --> 00:20:04.620
onto the electrical outlet.

00:20:04.620 --> 00:20:07.520
Nora’s death doesn’t really involve
water at all, but it is shown to be raining

00:20:07.520 --> 00:20:08.520
during that scene.

00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:12.300
Kat’s death is not a result of water, she’s killed
when her airbag pushes her into a sharp object,

00:20:12.300 --> 00:20:16.810
but Rory’s death is the result of punctured
fuel tank drips into a storm drain, eventually

00:20:16.810 --> 00:20:19.970
causing a news van to explode and launch a
barbed wire fence at him.

00:20:19.970 --> 00:20:23.130
Then there’s Kimberly, who has this plan
at the end that she’s going to tie and be

00:20:23.130 --> 00:20:26.550
resuscitated and she does this by driving
an ambulance into the lake.

00:20:26.550 --> 00:20:30.080
The two that I haven’t mentioned so far
are Eugene and Clear, who both die in an explosion

00:20:30.080 --> 00:20:33.320
that has nothing to do with water, but you
have to consider the reason they’re there

00:20:33.320 --> 00:20:36.580
in the first place is because Isabella, the
pregnant woman, has her water break.

00:20:36.580 --> 00:20:39.460
BURKE: “Seems like a bit of a reach don’t
you think?”

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:40.700
Maybe, Burke, maybe.

00:20:40.700 --> 00:20:44.660
That water break scene just has some of the
best acting I’ve ever seen in a movie.

00:20:44.660 --> 00:20:45.660
“My water.

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:46.660
It just broke.

00:20:46.660 --> 00:20:47.660
I’m gonna have my baby.”

00:20:47.660 --> 00:20:49.850
“No, not here, no, you… can’t do this
to me.”

00:20:49.850 --> 00:20:52.663
“Don’t just stand there, get me to a hospital.”

00:20:52.663 --> 00:20:54.530
“Just give me a second to think. Um.”

00:20:54.530 --> 00:21:00.082
Wow, just incredible performance, how did
this not win best supporting actor and actress?

00:21:00.082 --> 00:21:01.279
So realistic.

00:21:01.279 --> 00:21:02.423
So captivating.

00:21:02.423 --> 00:21:03.620
“Incredible job!”

00:21:03.620 --> 00:21:06.690
OK, I don’t want to spend this whole episode
just ragging on a movie.

00:21:06.690 --> 00:21:10.820
I do really like the concept of how all the
Route 23 people had their lives extended because

00:21:10.820 --> 00:21:13.450
the Flight 180 survivors lived longer than
they were supposed to.

00:21:13.450 --> 00:21:15.300
I just don’t get this part.

00:21:15.946 --> 00:21:18.283
“Wait a minute. Who are these people?”

00:21:18.283 --> 00:21:20.320
“The people who got off of Flight 180.”

00:21:20.320 --> 00:21:23.089
CLEAR: “They were my friends.”

00:21:23.358 --> 00:21:24.089
Hold up.

00:21:24.089 --> 00:21:25.214
Hold on a second.

00:21:25.214 --> 00:21:28.830
Let’s rewind to the first movie because
I certainly do not remember them being

00:21:28.830 --> 00:21:30.225
your friends, Clear.

00:21:31.391 --> 00:21:33.217
“Nobody forced you off the plane.

00:21:33.217 --> 00:21:35.269
You said you weren’t friends with those
that were.

00:21:35.269 --> 00:21:37.569
So Clear, why did you get off the plane?”

00:21:37.569 --> 00:21:40.000
“Because I saw and I heard Alex.”

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:43.300
Like I get that she became friends with Alex
and Carter at the end of the movie, but she

00:21:43.300 --> 00:21:44.940
can’t act like she was friends with all
of them.

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:47.160
And by the way, what is this picture in her
little padded room?

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:48.410
This never happened.

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:51.800
They were literally fighting with Terry and
Carter the moment before Terry died, there’s

00:21:51.800 --> 00:21:55.060
no point where this picture could possibly
exist; why you trying to rewrite the history

00:21:55.060 --> 00:21:56.060
of the first one?

00:21:56.060 --> 00:21:57.430
I don’t want to be too negative.

00:21:57.430 --> 00:22:00.400
There are actually some good scenes in this
movie.

00:22:02.984 --> 00:22:12.540
RORY: And if I die, would you throw out all
my drugs and my paraphernalia and my porno?

00:22:12.540 --> 00:22:16.800
Anything that’s gonna break my Mom’s heart.”

00:22:16.800 --> 00:22:19.050
That’s actually a really heartfelt moment.

00:22:19.050 --> 00:22:22.530
That makes me want to root for this guy to
survive and get his life together.

00:22:22.530 --> 00:22:25.418
But unfortunately, he’s dead 1 minute and
thirty four seconds later.

00:22:30.730 --> 00:22:34.220
Not long after we find out that the entire
objective of this movie was a lie, because

00:22:34.220 --> 00:22:37.280
Isabella was never supposed to die in the
pile-up in the first place, and Kimberly has

00:22:37.280 --> 00:22:41.500
another vision, and sees a new sign, an article
that says, “New Life For Drowning Victim.”

00:22:41.500 --> 00:22:45.140
If you read the article it seems to be about
another Final Destination-like event, where

00:22:45.140 --> 00:22:47.920
these two guys just happened to be at the
right place at the right time to save this

00:22:47.920 --> 00:22:49.380
woman who had nearly drowned.

00:22:49.380 --> 00:22:50.650
One of them is quoted in the article.

00:22:50.650 --> 00:22:54.150
“I wanted to stop at the Corn Dog Shop which
is one the other side of the hospital but

00:22:54.150 --> 00:22:55.300
Paul said, “No way!

00:22:55.300 --> 00:22:56.300
We’re goin’ to Dumpy’s.

00:22:56.300 --> 00:22:57.840
In two years we’ve never gone to Dumpy’s.

00:22:57.840 --> 00:23:00.640
I don’t know how to account for why we suddenly
changed our plans.”

00:23:00.640 --> 00:23:04.900
It sounds like maybe one of them had a vision
or saw a sign that influenced their behaviour,

00:23:04.900 --> 00:23:06.960
just like every Final Destination opening.

00:23:06.960 --> 00:23:11.070
And in true Final Destination fashion, these
two guys are named after new members of the

00:23:11.070 --> 00:23:12.070
movie.

00:23:12.070 --> 00:23:15.590
So, as I mentioned, Kimberly drives into the
lake, and is brought back by the paramedics.

00:23:15.590 --> 00:23:17.896
“Ready, clear.”

00:23:17.896 --> 00:23:19.470
No you got it all wrong.

00:23:19.470 --> 00:23:20.470
Clear’s the dead one.

00:23:20.470 --> 00:23:21.470
This is Kimberly.

00:23:21.470 --> 00:23:24.990
The final scene is this dinner scene with
the family of the farmer whose land they crashed

00:23:24.990 --> 00:23:26.510
on when their tires blew out.

00:23:26.510 --> 00:23:30.580
So they run a car into this dude’s farm,
cause all kinds of havoc and trouble, nearly

00:23:30.580 --> 00:23:34.300
get his son run over by a news van and he
responds by... trusting them with his truck

00:23:34.300 --> 00:23:36.420
when they just met, then inviting them over
for dinner?

00:23:36.420 --> 00:23:39.980
In any event way back towards the beginning
of this video, I mentioned all the references

00:23:39.980 --> 00:23:41.960
to luck, chance and misfortune.

00:23:41.960 --> 00:23:45.020
And when the farmer’s wife learns of how
her some narrowly avoided getting hit by a

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:49.790
van thanks to Rory’s intervention, she speaks
the final line of the movie.

00:23:49.790 --> 00:23:53.325
“You never told me that Peter.

